2026-11-04T07:20:09.6687218Z [1m== The Confidence view's per-grade rows — four swatches with a colour-blind-safe set, Tint/Ghost/Dither, opacity 0-100 and a count per grade, none rebuilding the scene (T-2648)[0m
2026-11-04T07:20:09.6739547Z T-2648 — the Confidence view per-grade rows
2026-11-04T07:20:09.6740351Z   ok   four swatches per grade, the first the grade colour (gold, silver, bronze), one set colour-blind safe
2026-11-04T07:20:09.6741756Z   ok   the colour-blind-safe set stays apart under protanopia, deuteranopia and tritanopia
2026-11-04T07:20:09.6743430Z   ok   every set keeps its three grades apart, and every row its four swatches, to ordinary vision
2026-11-04T07:20:09.6744862Z   ok   every swatch, look and row word is in the string table, and none is an id
2026-11-04T07:20:09.6746364Z   ok   each swatch reads back as itself off the renderer (the hex survives the colour space)
2026-11-04T07:20:09.6747340Z   ok   a swatch, a look or an opacity changes the scene: the colouring comes on, and a hidden grade is shown
2026-11-04T07:20:09.6748286Z   ok   opacity is a whole percent from 0 to 100; a bad look or value is refused and changes nothing
2026-11-04T07:20:09.6749157Z   ok   the colour-blind-safe set goes on all three grades in one, and every preset keeps it
